WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.550
- All right, let's finish
up with something cool

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.170
and different trending on social media.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.571
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.220
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.290
An Iowa banker is trending on TikTok

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.080
for one of the most unusual
hobbies I've ever heard of.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.870
He cleans and restores graves.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.390
Wade actually visits cemeteries
all over the country,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.390
removing mold, repairing
cracked and broken headstones

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.880
and bringing back the dignity
to those who have passed.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.050
It's such a beautiful thing.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.610
We have him on the line right now watching

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.380
on KCCI Des Moines.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.971
Hi, Wade, how are you doing?

00:00:29.971 --> 00:00:31.170
(audience cheering)

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.580
- Hey, Kelly, it's awesome to see you.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.750
Thanks for having me.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.190
- [Kelly] No, thank you
for what you're doing.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.300
It's such a beautiful thing.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.880
But how did you get into this?

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.930
- (laughs) Yeah, it's
an interesting story.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.130
It was from my grandfather.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.680
So like 25, 30 years ago,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.690
we were having a family reunion.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.040
And after the picnic lunch,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.540
we went over to the cemetery,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.850
and he said, "I think we should try

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.870
and clean the headstones."

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.340
And we were looking at the family,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.340
and it was my great-grandfather
and other relatives.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.880
And so he said it, but we
never followed through.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.080
So years later, I learned to
clean, I learned to reset,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.250
and then it really snowballed

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.160
into nearly a million
followers on social media.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.160
And in 2022, I traveled
20,000 miles over 16 states

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.050
and I really self-funded a
big project of trying to clean

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.749
and restore as many graves as possible.

00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:21.477
- That's such a beautiful thing to do,

00:01:21.477 --> 00:01:24.030
for not only those that have
passed, but their families.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.770
It seems so meaningful for the families,

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:28.020
but you say it's also meaningful
to you as well, right?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.790
- [Wade] It is, it really is.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.970
Alicia in your earlier
segment was talking about

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.220
a mentally safe place
in cleaning up parks.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.780
For me, it was seven years ago,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.990
I was in grad school and I
was addicted to Adderall.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.000
And after recovering from that,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.030
I was looking for a place and a way

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.170
to continue a mentally
safe place, peaceful,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.030
and so I got into working in cemeteries.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.490
And it was just an amazing space for me

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.250
to be able to share that with my followers

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.520
and reflect and remember other people.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.790
Everyone has a story
no matter who they are.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.430
And so working on their graves,
discovering who they were,

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.830
and then sharing that with my followers.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.850
And so it's been really awesome

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.770
to be able to see the descendants

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.480
of those people show up in my comments

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.880
and just be so excited to see the work

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.860
that's been done restoring and caring

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.950
for the gravestones of the
people that have passed.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.770
- What, first of all, thank
you for sharing your story,

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:25.020
and what an incredible
thing to find purpose

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.350
and passion out of something
that's so difficult

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.270
and challenging to overcome.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.470
Way to think outside of yourself

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.350
and do something amazing for other people.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.610
I'm such a fan of you, Wade.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.960
Thank you so much for joining us today.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.865
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:38.865 --> 00:02:40.080
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.945
- [Wade] Awesome, thank you, Kelly.

00:02:41.945 --> 00:02:43.110
- Well, and that's not all, my man.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.610
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.950
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the "Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.860
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, man,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.046
so they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:53.843
How's that sound?

00:02:53.843 --> 00:02:56.040
- Oh my God, thank you so much.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.210
I really appreciate that.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.860
That is gonna be amazing.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.290
Gonna put that to good use, thank you.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.650
- [Kelly] Aw man, thank you, Wade.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.180
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.790
Giancarlo Esposito, Brandon Scott Jones,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.820
Priyanka Naik, Hailey
Whitters, and Alicia.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.653
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:11.203
If it's not, try and change it.

